  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Amazonian communication for social transformation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will help raise awareness of the importance of the Pan-Amazon region in terms of biodiversity, natural resources, indigenous cultures, defence of rights and socio-environmental justice. REPAM seeks to create articulation mechanisms to promote communication that emphasises the ecological and socio-environmental values of the region, as well as making visible and promoting their culture, traditional knowledge and wisdom of the region&apos;s indigenous peoples and traditional communities.
The project will pay attention to ecological and sustainable land use practices, worldviews and cultural identity, as well as the defence and guarantee of human, collective and natural rights. It is about promoting actions that have a positive impact on society&apos;s awareness, attitudes and behaviours towards the Amazon region, contributing to the preservation of biodiversity, sustainable development and the cultural appreciation of local populations.</narrative>
  </description>
